WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:51.225
Purpose and scope. 1. Priorities and deliverables. Lindiwe confirms the current priority list and identifies decisions that require her attention. Daniel translates the list into a programme, preparation requirements, an action register and review points. For the Monday example, the decision pack and 09:30 preparation period are protected. Daniel identifies missing inputs; he does not approve the substantive financial or operational papers himself. 2. Scope of work. Daniel coordinates the diary, routine correspondence, meeting preparation, travel administration, relevant supplier follow-up and the administrative interfaces with the EPO and control room. Office facilities remain with the office-services owner. Contract interpretation remains with the designated legal or procurement owner. Public statements remain with the authorised communications function. Substantive business decisions stay with their appointed owners.
